# KEYS: zathura

## Basic Movement

- **h / j / k / l**: Move left / down / up / right in document
- **d / u**: Scroll down / up a half page
- **gg**: Go to the top of the document
- **G**: Go to the bottom of the document
- **f**: Highlight URLs to follow (follow mode)

---

## Zooming and View

- **J / K**: Zoom out / in
- **s**: Zoom to fit width
- **a**: Zoom to fit height
- **D**: Toggle dual-page mode
- **R**: Rotate document clockwise

---

## File Operations

- **r**: Reload document if changed
- **p**: Print document
- **o**: Open a new document
- **f**: Search for text in the document
- **q**: Quit zathura

---

## Command Mode (Ex Commands)

- **:open <path>**: Open a file from the specified path
- **:write <path>**: Save the current document to a new path
- **:export <path>**: Export the current document (e.g., to an image)
- **:set <option>**: Change settings dynamically (e.g., `:set statusbar-hiding true`)
- **:help**: Open the manual page

---

## Configuration Example

Zathura settings are typically stored in `~/.config/zathura/zathurarc`.

```conf
set selection-clipboard clipboard
set statusbar-hiding true
set guioptions none

# Custom Colors
set completion-bg "#1d2021"
set completion-fg "#ebdbb2"
set statusbar-bg "#1d2021"
set statusbar-fg "#ebdbb2"
```

